    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d888">

                <pb facs="0964" n="862" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg862"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/870: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at San
                        José</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Chase</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-12T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 12,
                                1919, 2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>At the suggestion of the Department of State Julio Acosta intends, the Department
                    is informed, to proceed with his friends to San José unarmed. Give this
                    information to Barquero immediately and inform him that Acosta’s proposed action
                    would seem materially to reduce danger of disorders and open the way for the
                    early holding of general elections as proposed by resolution mentioned in your
                    September 2, 9 a.m.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d888-f1"/></p>
                <p>Cable Department Barquero’s reply to the above.</p>
                <p>Confidential. Report by cable whether Barquero is in full command of the
                    situation, and whether Quirós is working loyally with him.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
